From: OpenATV STB Kodi Team <oe.patch@openatv.example>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] GLES: force GLES2 on Broadcom NXPL ARM platforms

Kodi requests an EGL_CONTEXT_CLIENT_VERSION 2 context on the STB windowing
backend and all supported Vu+/GigaBlue NXPL ARM recipes build with
OPENGLES_FORCE_GLES2. Their V3D drivers can nevertheless report OpenGL ES 3.x
through GL_VERSION, which makes Kodi select GLES3 shaders and texture handling
at runtime. This corrupts GUI image colour/alpha while the separate font path
remains intact.

Keep the actual driver string in the graphics log, but consistently expose
GLES 2.0 to Kodi's renderer selection on these Broadcom receivers.

diff --git a/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp b/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
--- a/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/rendering/gles/RenderSystemGLES.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,17 @@ bool CRenderSystemGLES::InitRenderSystem()
       sscanf(ver, "%*s %*s %d.%d", &m_RenderVersionMajor, &m_RenderVersionMinor);
     m_RenderVersion = ver;
   }
+#if defined(TARGET_VUPLUS_ARM) || defined(TARGET_GB)
+  if (m_RenderVersionMajor >= 3)
+  {
+    CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+              "Broadcom NXPL GLES compatibility: driver reports {}, forcing Kodi's GLES 2.0 "
+              "renderer path",
+              m_RenderVersion);
+    m_RenderVersionMajor = 2;
+    m_RenderVersionMinor = 0;
+  }
+#endif
 
   // Get our driver vendor and renderer
   const char *tmpVendor = (const char*) glGetString(GL_VENDOR);
